WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:03.100
- [Man] At midnight,
you have to play a game.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:03.933
- [Woman] Why?

00:00:03.933 --> 00:00:05.330
- It's just something
we do when someone new

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:06.400
joins the family.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.233
- A game?

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:09.523
What game?

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:11.570
- All right, so we're gonna start off

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.730
with the horrifying children's
games, because obviously

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.620
this is a horrifying
version of hide-and-go-seek.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.340
So, Chutes and Ladders, how
would you make it horrifying?

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.640
- Real, wait, are there snakes in there?

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.803
- I can't remember, I
remember Snakes and Ladders.

00:00:22.803 --> 00:00:24.870
- [Jacqueline] There's
Snakes and Ladders too, so.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.641
- So we can just put snakes
in Chutes and Ladders.

00:00:27.641 --> 00:00:28.474
- There you go.

00:00:28.474 --> 00:00:30.620
- How about a goat dungeon?

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.619
- Oh, a goat dungeon, with the ladder.

00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:33.710
Mmm.

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:34.547
Without a ladder.

00:00:34.547 --> 00:00:35.380
- Um.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.330
(laughing)

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:37.163
I have no idea.

00:00:37.163 --> 00:00:38.550
How do you make that more scary?

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.383
I just like snakes and ladders.

00:00:39.383 --> 00:00:40.667
- [Woman] What is Chutes and Ladders?

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:41.500
- I don't know. (laughs)

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.333
That's basically what we're hearing.

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:45.070
- [Interviewer] I mean
you climb up the ladder.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:47.010
- It's been a long time
since I've played this game.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:47.843
- Yeah.

00:00:47.843 --> 00:00:48.676
- But I'm aware of it.

00:00:48.676 --> 00:00:50.890
- You climb up the ladder, and
then if you get on the chute

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:52.641
that means that you lose
and you go to the bottom.

00:00:52.641 --> 00:00:55.370
But I think if maybe the
ladders had like knives on it,

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:56.310
instead of rungs.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:58.050
- What if the chutes had snakes in it?

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.056
- [Interviewer] Yeah, yeah, there you go.

00:01:00.056 --> 00:01:01.087
(laughs)

00:01:01.087 --> 00:01:01.940
- I got really excited about that.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:04.730
- So, so this one's a
little bit more for you,

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.540
Samara, but, What's the Time Mr. Wolf?

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.940
Did you play that as a kid?
- Oh yeah!

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:12.120
- That's an Australian game,
it's similar to our version

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.330
of Red Light, Green Light,

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:15.860
but how could you make
What's the Time Mr. Wolf--

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:17.590
- Real wolves?
- Real wolves.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:18.423
- More snakes.

00:01:18.423 --> 00:01:19.850
(laughing)
- There you go.

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:21.852
- That's good, she's
getting the same thing.

00:01:21.852 --> 00:01:22.910
- Alright, I don't think
you can bring snakes

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:24.600
to Monopoly, to make it more horrifying.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.161
- Well, (laughing) you would think.

00:01:27.161 --> 00:01:29.320
- [Jacqueline] What would
you do for Monopoly?

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.260
- To scare kids?
- Yes, to make it terrifying.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:32.460
- Some evil billionaires.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.362
- Oh, that's--
- Truly evil.

00:01:35.362 --> 00:01:36.252
- Billionaires.
- Who are kids,

00:01:36.252 --> 00:01:39.243
and who are bullies.
- They are big bullies,

00:01:39.243 --> 00:01:41.610
big bullies.
- That feels so similar

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:42.443
to things.

00:01:42.443 --> 00:01:43.276
Anyway (laughs).

00:01:44.219 --> 00:01:45.204
- Don't say that.

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:47.080
What about tag?

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.590
How would you make Tag horrifying?

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:49.450
- Snakes.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.013
- Snakes, yeah.

00:01:51.013 --> 00:01:51.846
(laughing)

00:01:51.846 --> 00:01:53.170
You tag them with a snake.

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:54.100
- There you go.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.470
- That's actually brilliant.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:56.303
Alright.

00:01:57.629 --> 00:01:59.690
Operation?

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:00.523
- Hmm.

00:02:00.523 --> 00:02:02.603
- Get children to do the operation.

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:05.763
- [Jacqueline] Oh my God, you
are really good at this game.

00:02:05.763 --> 00:02:06.775
- Blood bath.

00:02:06.775 --> 00:02:11.220
- Leave stuff in the
body, like, add nails,

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.550
put nails inside.
- That's actually good.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:16.350
Like, bad operation, like--
- Yeah, terrible operation.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.380
- I think there's a video game like that.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:18.485
- You guys are crazy.

00:02:18.485 --> 00:02:19.800
(laughing)

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:20.930
That's good.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:21.763
- I like that one.

00:02:21.763 --> 00:02:22.630
Okay, couple more.

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:23.853
Duck, Duck, Goose.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:27.128
- Real ducks.
- Duck, Duck, Death.

00:02:27.128 --> 00:02:28.057
(laughing)

00:02:28.057 --> 00:02:29.090
- Duck, Duck, Death!

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.260
You have to shoot the duck.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:31.331
(laughing)

00:02:31.331 --> 00:02:32.164
- What?
- Well, Duck, Duck,

00:02:32.164 --> 00:02:33.674
that's the one where you hit
'em on the top of the head,

00:02:33.674 --> 00:02:35.850
so maybe you like--
- Yeah.

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:36.700
- With water guns?

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.230
Oh, well bop 'em.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:39.114
That's even meaner.

00:02:39.114 --> 00:02:40.305
(laughing)

00:02:40.305 --> 00:02:41.203
- Bop 'em?
(laughing)

00:02:41.203 --> 00:02:43.130
And you call it Bop 'Em?
- Yeah, like, cause you know,

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:43.990
you go Duck, Duck,

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.490
and you're suppose to do it softly,

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:47.253
but like, you could like--

00:02:47.253 --> 00:02:48.086
- Yeah, have a hammer
- Really hit 'em,

00:02:48.086 --> 00:02:50.090
with a snake!
(laughing)

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:51.330
Strangle 'em with a snake.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:54.313
- Alright, if y'all can
work in snake to Hot Potato.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.550
- It's not a potato anymore, is it?

00:02:57.550 --> 00:02:58.383
- Snake Potato.

00:02:58.383 --> 00:03:00.287
- Snake Potato.
(laughing)

00:03:00.287 --> 00:03:01.450
- I would eat that.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:02.570
(laughing)

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:03.640
- Snake potato?

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:04.900
Do they eat snakes in Australia?

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:06.190
- No.
- Okay.

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:07.220
- I know some places do.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.053
- Some people do, yeah.

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:10.190
- I'm just, just curious, I've seen this.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.400
But, alright, that's it.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.272
I didn't think Australia
was some crazy land, but..

00:03:13.272 --> 00:03:14.105
(laughing)

00:03:14.105 --> 00:03:15.121
you said you wanted to eat it so.

00:03:15.121 --> 00:03:17.615
(laughing)

00:03:17.615 --> 00:03:18.448
- Have I eaten a snake before?

00:03:18.448 --> 00:03:19.281
I don't think so.

00:03:19.281 --> 00:03:20.820
- This sort of premise
begins at a wedding,

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:23.783
so what's your worst wedding horror story?

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.385
- I mean how many
weddings have you been to?

00:03:27.385 --> 00:03:28.253
- A few.

00:03:28.253 --> 00:03:29.086
- Have you?

00:03:29.086 --> 00:03:29.919
- Do you have a good one?

00:03:29.919 --> 00:03:30.752
- I'm tryin' to think--

00:03:30.752 --> 00:03:31.585
- A good horror story?

00:03:31.585 --> 00:03:33.350
I mean usually there's
someone that gets drunk.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.520
- Divorced?

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.910
(laughing)

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:37.381
- People do get drunk a lot.

00:03:37.381 --> 00:03:39.539
- They get drunk.

00:03:39.539 --> 00:03:41.940
- I don't know if I can say
without offending people

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:42.773
at my (laughs).

00:03:42.773 --> 00:03:43.606
- Say it, say it!

00:03:43.606 --> 00:03:44.439
- I know, that's what I was thinking.

00:03:44.439 --> 00:03:45.770
- Depends on how bad it is.
- They won't watch this

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:47.244
I promise you.

00:03:47.244 --> 00:03:48.170
(laughing)

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:49.193
- What happened, what happened?

00:03:49.193 --> 00:03:52.010
- There was a really sad bridesmaid,

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:55.130
who made a speech about her break up

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.997
and, like, the room just cleared.

00:03:57.997 --> 00:04:00.103
It was really sad and awkward.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:01.893
- Was she drinking?

00:04:01.893 --> 00:04:03.280
- Yeah.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:05.190
- Well, I'm from the south,
I could tell you about

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:07.324
a lot of rednecks that
get drunk at weddings.

00:04:07.324 --> 00:04:08.520
(laughs)

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.650
- Sometimes shot guns, I'm from Alabama.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.238
- Okay, well you know then.
- Yes (laughs)

00:04:12.238 --> 00:04:14.759
- You know, it's a good
excuse to like, let go.

00:04:14.759 --> 00:04:16.379
- Yeah.

00:04:16.379 --> 00:04:18.331
- Free food and cake.

00:04:18.331 --> 00:04:19.164
(laughing)

00:04:19.164 --> 00:04:21.130
- I find that people who
can't wrap up the speech.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.687
There always like, "oh
my god, me and Diane,

00:04:23.687 --> 00:04:24.977
"we were best friends,

00:04:24.977 --> 00:04:26.827
"we used to call each other cookie sisters

00:04:26.827 --> 00:04:27.873
"because, oh, whatever."

00:04:27.873 --> 00:04:29.387
And then at the end they're like,

00:04:29.387 --> 00:04:30.897
"Anyway, I love you so much,

00:04:30.897 --> 00:04:34.787
"I love Ben, Ben's great, I love you guys,

00:04:34.787 --> 00:04:37.544
"so much, I love you guys,"

00:04:37.544 --> 00:04:38.565
(laughing)

00:04:38.565 --> 00:04:40.365
and I'm like, "Oh my god,
just give me the dessert!"

00:04:40.365 --> 00:04:41.323
- The cookie sisters!

00:04:41.323 --> 00:04:42.672
- Good job, Mark, that's good.

00:04:42.672 --> 00:04:43.505
- It's not bad.

00:04:43.505 --> 00:04:44.338
- That's very good.

00:04:44.338 --> 00:04:45.171
- It's good.

00:04:45.171 --> 00:04:46.004
- That is a very good impression

00:04:46.004 --> 00:04:46.837
of a horrible wedding speech.

00:04:46.837 --> 00:04:47.763
- That was his speech.

00:04:47.763 --> 00:04:49.130
(laughing)

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:50.900
- And that's my general,
kinda way of speaking.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.520
- No, and I just wanna
add the comedy of asking

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.430
that to the woman that starred

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:55.580
in, "Four Weddings and a Funeral"

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:57.049
is definitely not lost.

00:04:57.049 --> 00:04:57.913
(laughing)

00:04:57.913 --> 00:04:59.296
- Great speeches, though, great speeches.

00:04:59.296 --> 00:05:00.750
- Great speeches in that movie.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.330
Did you guys get to play
hide and seek on set?

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.320
Like, I figure like you have to right,

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.990
to just do some kind of game?

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:09.907
- [Andie] You guys were
playin' games the whole time.

00:05:09.907 --> 00:05:11.330
But they just did like, word games.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:12.820
- [Samara] Yeah, Mark has this crazy game,

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:14.740
that makes you want to kill yourself.

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:15.770
(laughing)

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:16.813
- [Mark] Yeah, it's not dark as that.

00:05:16.813 --> 00:05:17.646
(laughing)

00:05:17.646 --> 00:05:18.479
- [Host] Mark?

00:05:18.479 --> 00:05:19.820
- That was just how you
reacted to the game.

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:21.234
- I'd get so annoyed.

00:05:21.234 --> 00:05:22.510
- It's a really nerdy game, it's like,

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.432
it's so nerdy.
- it's very nerdy.

00:05:24.432 --> 00:05:26.840
- You come up with the
word, it's five letters,

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:29.640
no repeating letters, and
then the person has to guess

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.552
how many, it's just so bad.

00:05:31.552 --> 00:05:32.385
But that's what we played.

00:05:32.385 --> 00:05:33.218
- It's a word game.

00:05:33.218 --> 00:05:35.490
- Did you like, text it
to each other, or like?

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.323
- At the end, I'd just be like,

00:05:36.323 --> 00:05:37.156
"I need to get this word right."

00:05:37.156 --> 00:05:37.989
- You used to be really upset, like,

00:05:37.989 --> 00:05:39.627
and it'd be a big scene,
and you'd be like,

00:05:39.627 --> 00:05:40.540
"hang on a second,"

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:41.650
- Well 'cause some people would get it

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.881
in like six guesses and I had five pages,

00:05:44.881 --> 00:05:45.714
- But then you got good!

00:05:45.714 --> 00:05:46.969
- And Mark was like, nope, nope.

00:05:46.969 --> 00:05:48.890
I did get better.

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:50.600
- Didn't we play something else?

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.870
- We played. (laughing)

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.245
- Oh, yeah. (laughing)

00:05:53.245 --> 00:05:55.578
- [Andie] What did you play?

00:05:56.826 --> 00:05:57.978
- You gonna make that public?

00:05:57.978 --> 00:05:58.811
- Oh no.

00:05:58.811 --> 00:06:01.768
- [Andie] Yes you have to
now, the audience will be mad.

00:06:01.768 --> 00:06:02.601
- Play it with me, show it.

00:06:02.601 --> 00:06:04.240
- So me and my sister when
we were really little,

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:05.960
we made up this game, and we,

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.640
for lack of a better word, we were little,

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.500
so we called it the elephant game,

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:12.516
and I showed Mark and we played.

00:06:12.516 --> 00:06:13.349
(laughing)

00:06:13.349 --> 00:06:15.506
Basically, your hands become elephants.

00:06:15.506 --> 00:06:17.248
- So yeah, so, these are elephants.

00:06:17.248 --> 00:06:20.740
- And then you have to walk
and try to get the other

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:21.728
person's nail,

00:06:21.728 --> 00:06:22.561
- So you get me,

00:06:22.561 --> 00:06:23.488
- And they like, fly.

00:06:23.488 --> 00:06:24.407
- And then I'm dead.

00:06:24.407 --> 00:06:25.708
(laughing)

00:06:25.708 --> 00:06:27.570
- And that's it.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:28.498
- That is a great game.

00:06:28.498 --> 00:06:30.120
- Big in Australia.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:31.093
- Big in Australia?

00:06:31.093 --> 00:06:33.812
- Yeah, big with just me and Morgan.

00:06:33.812 --> 00:06:35.092
(laughing)

00:06:35.092 --> 00:06:35.950
- And now me.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:37.100
- And now you, I like that.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.250
I definitely like that.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:41.280
So, there's a lot of like
prosthetics, and blood

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:43.420
and like practical effects in the film,

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:46.390
