00:07:42.737 --> 00:07:43.570
- Mmm.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:45.150
(laughing)

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:46.350
- So this is my next question,

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:48.760
'cause this is not the type
of film I've seen you in,

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.717
normally, like I said, so was this like,

00:07:50.717 --> 00:07:53.610
alright I wanna go genre, or what exactly

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.906
made you be like let's go
get bloody, let's go get--

00:07:55.906 --> 00:07:57.600
- It was a great script.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:02.600
It's a really well written,
fun, and it's a brilliant idea,

00:08:02.836 --> 00:08:07.836
it's extremely clever, and it
has also a lot of humor in it,

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:12.910
so it's not your typical horror movie,

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:15.270
like you're so scared,
even though there are a lot

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:19.333
of moments where you are scared,
and there's amazing gore,

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:21.970
it's really bright and funny

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:25.690
and has comic timing,

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:28.320
and opportunity for great comic timing,

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:31.160
and fun to get to work

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:34.100
with wonderful, beautiful, young people.

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:36.785
The first scene I did was,

00:08:36.785 --> 00:08:37.618
- I whacked her in the head.

00:08:37.618 --> 00:08:39.640
- We fought, we got in a
fight, we had to fight,

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:42.660
I'd never been in a fight,
so I was winging it,

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.590
just trying to figure out how to do it.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:46.440
- You were great, but
I hit you in the head.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.387
- You were fabulous, you're a pro.

00:08:48.387 --> 00:08:49.683
- But in rehearsals, you had a bump.

00:08:49.683 --> 00:08:50.516
- I know you did hit me

00:08:50.516 --> 00:08:51.349
(laughing)

00:08:51.349 --> 00:08:53.150
- But I told Cynthia, the night you gave

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:54.620
me a black eye, then I remembered,

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:56.423
oh, it wasn't a black eye,
but it was a good story.

00:08:56.423 --> 00:08:57.256
- Oh my gosh, did I give you a black eye?

00:08:57.256 --> 00:08:58.220
- No you didn't give me a black eye,

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:00.410
but it was a bruise, I had an egg,

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.266
you know how sensitive your forehead is?

00:09:02.266 --> 00:09:03.099
- It was like, "Hi nice
to meet you, Andie"

00:09:03.099 --> 00:09:03.932
and then bff.

00:09:03.932 --> 00:09:05.510
- She gave me an egg, she gave me an egg.

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:07.960
But what was really funny,
thinking back on it,

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:09.190
if you think back on it,

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:13.300
is they weren't really
helping us at first, right?

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:16.540
So we were like in this room,
with a pad and all that,

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:18.860
trying to figure out how we
were gonna do this fight scene,

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:21.350
and we were just, both of us are like,

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:26.191
gonna go out at it 100%, you
know, no hold back, right?

00:09:26.191 --> 00:09:29.240
Even this like figuring
out, we're goin' right?

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:31.050
We're professionals here.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:32.133
We're gonna kill each other.

00:09:32.133 --> 00:09:33.443
(laughing)

00:09:33.443 --> 00:09:35.290
And then, they had to
stop the whole thing,

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:37.080
and they were like no, no, no stop,

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:38.900
they made everyone leave the room.

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:41.516
It was very dramatic, you know, calm down.

00:09:41.516 --> 00:09:42.756
- Was that first day of filming?

00:09:42.756 --> 00:09:43.589
That was the very first day.

00:09:43.589 --> 00:09:44.536
- This is like, just rehearsing.

00:09:44.536 --> 00:09:46.220
This was just the rehearsal for the scene,

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:47.053
- It was the first--

00:09:47.053 --> 00:09:49.670
- Then I got boxed in the
head, it was an accident,

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:50.813
but the drama behind it.

00:09:50.813 --> 00:09:53.110
- Well yeah, they thought maybe

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:55.366
Andie Macdowell's gonna leave.

00:09:55.366 --> 00:09:56.199
(laughing)

00:09:56.199 --> 00:09:57.785
- Oh no, no, no!

00:09:57.785 --> 00:09:58.618
- [Host] She's a trooper.

00:09:58.618 --> 00:09:59.451
- I just, I had a little egg.

00:09:59.451 --> 00:10:00.284
- We know that, yeah.

00:10:00.284 --> 00:10:02.223
- I just knew that if we
put ice on it right away,

00:10:02.223 --> 00:10:03.550
have you ever had one of those?

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:05.500
- I have had one of those,
but I'm normally the person

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.610
that walks around with a
baseball bat on my forehead

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:09.500
for a week and half 'cause I didn't think

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:10.333
of the ice thing right away.

00:10:10.333 --> 00:10:12.230
- Yeah if you ice it, it'll go down.

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:15.230
- So that kinda brings
me to my next question,

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:18.010
did you guys have to do
like specific training

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.080
to get ready for it?

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:19.990
Like, nothing?

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:21.740
They just kinda threw you guys in there.

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:23.720
That sounds about ready
for this movie, actually.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.106
That makes a lot of sense.

00:10:25.106 --> 00:10:27.240
- We wanted it to look sloppy and messy

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:32.240
and the stunt team were really
great in keeping it look like

00:10:32.367 --> 00:10:36.750
we weren't fighters, but
making it very, very safe.

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:38.820
- Awesome, alright I have
just a couple more questions.

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:41.223
What was your favorite
hiding place as a kid?

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:44.693
Like in your house, or home?

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:49.480
- I used to love to hide outside.

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:52.350
We used to play sardines or kick the can.

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:53.183
- Mm-hm.

00:10:53.183 --> 00:10:55.010
- Which was one of my, did
you ever play kick the can?

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:55.843
- Kick the can?

00:10:55.843 --> 00:10:56.676
No.

00:10:56.676 --> 00:10:57.509
- So much fun.

00:10:57.509 --> 00:10:58.440
Well you know, you played kick the can?

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:01.189
- Yeah, well it's a version
kind of, I guess like,

00:11:01.189 --> 00:11:04.200
kinda like hide and seek but
not really, it's more like,

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.700
sardines is hide and seek
almost exactly, right?

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.504
Sardines you hid with them?
- Sardines, one person hides,

00:11:08.504 --> 00:11:10.843
and then you find them, and
get in with them, so much fun.

00:11:10.843 --> 00:11:11.676
- Yes, yes.

00:11:11.676 --> 00:11:13.060
- I love that game.

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:17.220
And kick the can is, one person's it,

00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:18.467
and you might do that,

00:11:18.467 --> 00:11:21.164
you remember that thing
you do with you hands?

00:11:21.164 --> 00:11:23.212
It used to be this thing
that you do with your hands?

00:11:23.212 --> 00:11:25.604
- Oh yeah, where you pick each other,

00:11:25.604 --> 00:11:26.723
eenie, meanie, mini

00:11:26.723 --> 00:11:27.556
- How you get the person's it.

00:11:27.556 --> 00:11:28.389
- Yeah.

00:11:28.389 --> 00:11:31.280
- Anyway, so the person
that's it has to count,

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:34.470
and you go hide, and then
you run in and kick the can,

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:36.885
and you're safe, so you
have to get to the can.

00:11:36.885 --> 00:11:37.718
- Oh.

00:11:37.718 --> 00:11:39.060
- It's like reverse, hide
and go, it's basically like

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:40.140
kinda like, get back here,

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:41.180
that kinda thing
- yeah, exactly.

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:42.429
- Before somebody catches you.

00:11:42.429 --> 00:11:45.012
(upbeat music)

